  "draftIsFinal": false,
  "summary": "I wrote `src/main.ts`. It typechecks, but I couldn't run `vite build` or open the scene in a browser, so none of it has been seen rendering. That includes the custom water shader, the per-frame sky updates and the camera orbit, which I wrote from the docs and type definitions.\n\n- **Island:** The terrain is a jittered 56×56 heightfield with a rounded coastline. It uses per-triangle flat normals and vertex colours: sand, two greens and rock. About 18 trees (pines and round-crown trees) and about 9 rocks are generated in code, with no model files.\n- **Water:** A 300-unit wave grid with a custom GLSL shader. It has three animated sine waves, a Fresnel mix with the sky colour, sun glint, and shallow-to-deep colour with animated foam rings along the coast. It fades into the horizon colour with distance, so its far edge isn't visible.\n- **Day/night:** A 20-second cycle sets the sun's elevation and azimuth. Each frame it updates:\n  - the Preetham sky (with stars) via `app.atmosphere.setSky`,\n  - the fog colour,\n  - the sun light's position, colour and intensity,\n  - a moon light that comes up when the sun goes down,\n  - the hemisphere light, and\n  - the water shader's uniforms.\n\n  The hemisphere light and moon keep the scene lit at night, so it is never black.\n- **Camera:** It orbits slowly at radius 40 and height 21, looking at the island, using `app.camera.setPose`.\n- **Ready flag:** `window.__EVAL_READY__` is set two animation frames after `app.ready()`.\n\n",
